From af10d6061d949f3c84d0edbfeba38dce8bd7b912 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:59:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] tests: pin scratch archive shape safety boundaries

Add the five regression tests requested after #2662: bare gitdir identity, private index isolation, gitlink re-signature, outside-gitdir unpushed commits, and bare metadata non-descent. The private-index probe forces an actual Git index write inside the archive-worktree seam and checks original bytes and nanosecond mtime.

Proof: canonical shape suite 25 passed. Original spec-2662.json (only execution paths/environment adapted) through mutants.py: all 15 mutants killed, zero survivors; each of E3/E5/E10/E11/E13 fails its named new regression. scripts/check: 20 checks ok.
---
